AR(1)                         User Commands

NAME
    ar - maintain archives of files

SYNOPSIS
    ar [-]{dpqrtx}[cousv] archive [member...]

DESCRIPTION
    Creates and modifies archives in the System V format that the GNU
    binutils write, so archives made on the host and on minios are
    interchangeable and make(1) can date lib.a(member.o) prerequisites.
    One operation letter is required: d deletes the named members, p
    prints them to standard output, q appends the files without checking
    for duplicates, r adds the files and replaces members of the same
    name in place, t lists the members, x extracts them into the current
    directory. Without member names t, p and x act on every member.

    The modifiers are c (do not report the creation of a new archive), o
    (extraction keeps the recorded modification time), u (r replaces a
    member only with a newer file), s (accepted; no symbol table is
    written) and v (verbose: a - added, r - replaced, d - deleted, x -
    extracted, and the mode, owner, size, date and name for t). A
    symbol table found in an archive is dropped when the archive is
    rewritten.

SEE ALSO
    make(1), tar(1), index(7)
